# PR Diff Truncated

Original size: 14906 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index e010a34bf5..12cc436aa2 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -13,6 +13,18 @@ block a release again.

 ## Unreleased

+- fix: `fileInfo().name` returns the bare entry name on Windows — the
+  abspath resolution previously glued the drive-letter absolute path onto
+  the returned name (`C:\dirC:\dir\file.txt`), breaking the file browser
+  listings and any consumer that joins `dir` + `name` back into a path.
+- fix(flutter_app): the Windows desktop app can pick a project folder —
+  a file-selector-backed `ProjectFolderOps` (the folder dialog through
+  `file_selector_windows`) for Windows/Linux instead of the macOS-only
+  method channel, the desktop env layers the project-mount wrapper on
+  every desktop platform (the mount previously existed on macOS only, so
+  a picked folder never reached the agent env), and the Windows runner
+  identity is real (window title "Fa", `CompanyName` "Fa" — the support
+  dir moves from `%APPDATA%\com.example\...` to `%APPDATA%\Fa\...`).
 - feat(gh-2098): the auto-compact trigger is user-configurable —
   `compaction.triggerRatio` / `compaction.reserveTokens` /
   `compaction.keepRecentTokens` in `~/.fah/config.yaml` or project
diff --git a/flutter_app/lib/sandbox/env_factory_io.dart b/flutter_app/lib/sandbox/env_factory_io.dart
index 86883bf60f..6b73f75a06 100644
--- a/flutter_app/lib/sandbox/env_factory_io.dart
+++ b/flutter_app/lib/sandbox/env_factory_io.dart
@@ -247,19 +247,21 @@ final class _MobileExecutionEnv extends PersistentWebExecutionEnv

 /// The desktop branch of [createPlatformEnv]: the application-support
 /// directory as the container cwd so settings/stores live inside the app
-/// sandbox and do not trigger a permission prompt on macOS. macOS
-/// additionally layers the optional project-folder mount on top via
-/// [mountedDesktopEnv].
+/// sandbox and do not trigger a permission prompt on macOS. Every desktop
+/// platform layers the optional project-folder mount on top via
+/// [mountedDesktopEnv] (the selector-backed pick on Windows/Linux — the
+/// channel/bookmark layer is macOS-only; see [defaultProjectFolderOps]).
 Future<ExecutionEnv> createDesktopEnv() async {
   final appDir = await getApplicationSupportDirectory();
   final baseEnv = LocalExecutionEnv(cwd: appDir.path);
-  if (!Platform.isMacOS) return baseEnv;
   return mountedDesktopEnv(baseEnv);
 }

-/// macOS project-folder mount layer over [baseEnv]: restores the persisted
-/// mount (bookmark access re-granted → [ProjectMountEnv.mountedRoot], or the
-/// stale-mount note when access is refused).
+/// The desktop project-folder mount layer over [baseEnv]: restores the
+/// persisted mount (access re-granted → [ProjectMountEnv.mountedRoot], or
+/// the stale-mount note when access is refused). Bookmark re-granting is
+/// macOS-only; Windows/Linux restore directly through the selector ops
+/// (no sandbox to re-grant — see [defaultProjectFolderOps]).
 Future<ExecutionEnv> mountedDesktopEnv(LocalExecutionEnv baseEnv) async {
   final mountEnv = ProjectMountEnv(baseEnv);
   final stored = await ProjectMountStore.load(baseEnv);
@@ -267,7 +269,9 @@ Future<ExecutionEnv> mountedDesktopEnv(LocalExecutionEnv baseEnv) async {
   applyStoredMount(
     mountEnv,
     stored,
-    granted: await ProjectFolderChannelOps().startAccessing(stored.bookmark),
+    granted:
+        await (defaultProjectFolderOps() ?? const ProjectFolderChannelOps())
+            .startAccessing(stored.bookmark),
   );
   return mountEnv;
 }
diff --git a/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart b/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart
index 4848cde516..cd37c8b37e 100644
--- a/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart
+++ b/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart'
     show TargetPlatform, defaultTargetPlatform, kIsWeb, visibleForTesting;

+import 'package:file_selector/file_selector.dart';
 import 'package:flutter/services.dart';

 /// Native project-folder operations: directory picking plus the
@@ -69,3 +70,42 @@ final class ProjectFolderChannelOps implements ProjectFolderOps {
     await _channel.invokeMethod<void>('stopAccessing', bookmark);
   }
 }
+
+/// The desktop file-selector-backed ops (Windows/Linux): the native folder
+/// dialog through `file_selector` (file_selector_windows is a compiled
+/// plugin in the Windows runner) without security-scoped bookmarks — the
+/// bookmark is always the empty string and the access lifecycle is a
+/// success no-op, matching how [ProjectMountStore] persists the mount on
+/// platforms that have no sandbox to re-grant.
+final class ProjectFolderSelectorOps implements ProjectFolderOps {
+  /// Creates the selector-backed ops.
+  const ProjectFolderSelectorOps();
+
+  @override
+  Future<({String path, String bookmark})?> pickDirectory() async {
+    final path = await getDirectoryPath();
+    if (path == null || path.isEmpty) return null;
+    return (path: path, bookmark: '');
+  }
+
+  @override
+  Future<bool> startAccessing(String bookmark) async => true;
+
+  @override
+  Future<void> stopAccessing(String bookmark) async {}
